<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Eagle Cry</h1>
<p>Sphere: Summoning Sphere
Class: Ranger (guild level 29)
Mana: 20
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>cast eagle cry</a>
</pre>
<p>The ranger calls out into the sky 'aquila!', and an eagle swoops down out 
of nowhere and alights on the ranger's shoulder. It follows you, and fights 
for you by itself: when you fight, it attacks your foe, and when your 
wounds grow serious, below a third of your hit points, it tries to rescue 
you. It never attacks another player unless both of you have signed the 
Book of Blood.
</p><p>The eagle stays only a short while, from a quarter of a minute to a little 
over a minute, the better your spell, and then flies away, its mission 
fulfilled. It needs the open sky: indoors, or wherever the weather doesn't 
reach, the spell can't be cast. You must be standing. It is also found on 
scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Summon Animal</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Summoning Sphere</a>
</pre>




</div>